From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0780: NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation (frame_generation=dlss) and Reflex through Streamline (Direct3D 12)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (DLSS study, $WORK/scratch/dlss/DESIGN.md). Streamline 2.14.16's public API (sl_dlss_g.h,
  sl_reflex.h, sl_pcl.h; ProgrammingGuideDLSS_G.md, ProgrammingGuideReflex.md, ProgrammingGuidePCL.md); headers from
  REXGLUE_STREAMLINE_DIR, outside the tree. Needs 0770
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause). NVIDIA's
  SDK and DLLs are never in the tree or the patch (as 0770)
Purpose: frame_generation=dlss runs NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation: 2x on an RTX 40, up to 6x (multi frame generation) where
  DLSSGState::numFramesToGenerateMax allows; cvars dlssg_frames (1-5 generated per rendered frame, live, lowered to the
  GPU's most), dlssg_debug (bits: state log every 300 frames, no HUD-less tag, only-generated view). With it at start,
  Streamline also loads sl.dlss_g, sl.reflex and sl.pcl, the direct queue is made through Streamline's proxy device (it
  hooks CreateCommandQueue; the SDK submits to the native interface), and the low-latency layer's backend is
  Streamline's Reflex (slReflexSetOptions / slReflexSleep / slPCLSetMarker; the NVAPI one cannot be used with DLSS-G),
  forced on by low_latency_frame_generation=auto as for AMD's. Frame ids are the low-latency layer's (the swap packet's
  ordinal), so the PCL markers, DLSS SR's evaluation and DLSS-G's constants name the same frame. Per guest frame, before
  its Present (D3D12Presenter::DlssgBeforePresent): the anti-aliasing pass's depth and motion vectors (render size) and,
  in SDR, the refresher's HUD-less image are tagged eValidUntilPresent, the camera the GPU command thread published for
  that frame id (streamline::PublishFrameConstants from TaaRun) is set with slSetConstants, and DLSSGOptions change only
  when they must (mode off for frames without an id, inputs or constants: logos, loads, menus without the 3D pass;
  eRetainResourcesWhenOff). The refresher gets frame generation's inputs through GetFrameGenerationInputs (no compose;
  the swap path itself is unchanged). AMD's frame generation is never made for dlss. Limits: the guest output must be
  shown 1:1 (2000p on 3200x2000, 1080p on 1920x1080; else off, logged once); no HUD-less image in HDR (another
  encoding); no UI alpha yet (needs the refresher to write it). The game must call LowLatency::OnFrameStart once per
  engine frame (mcla-x86's heartbeat hook does with this change on its side), else no frame has an id and DLSS-G stays
  off. Log lines: `Streamline: DLSS Frame Generation available, Reflex available`, `Low latency: NVIDIA Reflex through
  Streamline`, `DLSS Frame Generation: up to 2x on this GPU (...)`, `DLSS Frame Generation: on, 2x, output 3200x2000,
  depth and vectors 1600x1000`. NVIDIA's sl_pcl.h / sl_reflex.h 2.14.16 do not compile as C++23 (a `using` of
  std::to_underlying); d3d12_streamline.h includes them with __cplusplus pushed to C++20's. Not built before the next SDK
  build.
  Found by running it (RTX 4060 Laptop, 3200x2000 on the 165 Hz G-Sync panel): (1) FrameGenerationSwapChainActive() is true for dlss
  (PaintAndPresentImpl answered kNotPresentedConnectionOutdated to every paint otherwise: the swap chain was recreated in a loop and
  nothing was presented); (2) frame generation switches the UI layer separation on (SetFrameGenerationUiSeparation, as AMD's swap chain
  does): without it the refresher never writes the HUD-less image and the swap path gives no depth / vectors; (3) the proxy device
  UpgradeDevice makes is kept to the end (the proxy queue does not hold it; a freed one crashed sl.interposer's DXGISwapChain constructor
  in CreateSwapChainForHwnd on about every second start); (4) in SDR the swap path feeds frame generation only without FXAA and the game's
  piecewise linear gamma ramp: a minute of frames without inputs logs why; (5) streamline_log >= 1 installs a vectored handler that logs a
  crash's address and stack as module+offset (how (3) was found). Measured with it: 60 simulated frames shown as 118.7 a second,
  PresentMon Independent Flip with tearing (G-Sync), MsBetweenDisplayChange p50 8.35 / p99 11.4 ms, a 6 minute bench drive without a
  crash (36,956 presents, 1 % low 87.9 fps), live frame_generation off <-> dlss without a hitch, HUD intact in the generated frames
  (dlssg_debug=4). dlssg_debug bit 1 also logs what each of the first frames has. Needs 0770.
Bucket: REDO
---
